{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/separation-techniques/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/separation-techniques.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Separation Techniques | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-400 to-teal-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -filter text-cyan-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"filter_list\">filter_list</span>Separation Techniques\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Methods for separating mixtures and purifying substances in the laboratory.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-cyan-50 border-l-4 border-cyan-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-cyan-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-cyan-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Identify appropriate separation methods for different mixtures</li>\n          <li>• Describe filtration, distillation, evaporation, and crystallization</li>\n          <li>• Explain chromatography and its applications</li>\n          <li>• Understand fractional distillation and separating funnels</li>\n          <li>• Apply separation techniques to solve practical problems</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          Why Separate Mixtures?\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Mixtures can be separated because the components have different <strong class=\"text-cyan-600\">physical properties</strong> (size, boiling point, solubility, magnetism, etc.). The choice of method depends on the nature of the mixture.</p>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Solid-Solid Mixtures</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Hand picking, sieving, magnetic separation, sublimation</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Solid-Liquid Mixtures</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Filtration, evaporation, crystallization, centrifugation</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Liquid-Liquid Mixtures</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Separating funnel, fractional distillation</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Gas-Gas Mixtures</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Fractional distillation of liquid air</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Filtration -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Filtration\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-100 to-teal-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-cyan-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-cyan-800 mb-1\">Principle</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Separates an <strong class=\"text-cyan-600\">insoluble solid</strong> from a liquid using a filter that allows only the liquid to pass through.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-cyan-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -flask mr-2\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Apparatus</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Filter paper (folded into cone)</li>\n                <li>• Filter funnel</li>\n                <li>• Beaker/conical flask</li>\n                <li>• Glass rod (for pouring)</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-cyan-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -tag mr-2\" data-mi=\"sell\">sell</span>Terms</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• <strong>Residue:</strong> Solid left on filter paper</li>\n                <li>• <strong>Filtrate:</strong> Liquid that passes through</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Example</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Separating sand from water: Sand (residue) stays on filter paper, water (filtrate) passes through.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Distillation -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Distillation\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-100 to-indigo-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-1\">Principle</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Separates a <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">liquid from a solution</strong> by boiling, then condensing the vapor back to liquid.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -thermometer-half mr-2\" data-mi=\"device_thermostat\">device_thermostat</span>Simple Distillation</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">For separating a liquid from a dissolved solid (different boiling points).</p>\n              <p class=\"text-blue-600 text-sm mt-2\"><strong>Example:</strong> Obtaining pure water from salt solution</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -layer-group mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Fractional Distillation</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">For separating miscible liquids with close boiling points.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-purple-600 text-sm mt-2\"><strong>Example:</strong> Crude oil refining, liquid air separation</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -vial mr-2\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Apparatus</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Round-bottom flask</li>\n                <li>• Fractionating column</li>\n                <li>• Condenser</li>\n                <li>• Receiver</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-blue-50 text-left font-semibold text-blue-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-blue-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-blue-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Separating Ethanol and Water</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Ethanol boils at 78°C, water at 100°C. How do you separate them?</p>\n\n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Heat the mixture in a flask with a fractionating column</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Ethanol (lower boiling point) vaporizes first at 78°C</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Vapor passes through condenser and collects as pure ethanol</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Water remains in the flask (collected later)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Evaporation & Crystallization -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Evaporation &amp; Crystallization\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-100 to-yellow-100 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Evaporation</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">Used to recover a <strong class=\"text-orange-600\">dissolved solid</strong> from a solution by heating to evaporate the solvent.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-orange-600 text-sm\"><strong>Example:</strong> Obtaining salt from salt solution</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Note: Best for solids that don't decompose on heating</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-100 to-teal-100 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">Crystallization</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">Used for solids that <strong class=\"text-green-600\">decompose on heating</strong>. Solution is concentrated, then cooled slowly.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-green-600 text-sm\"><strong>Example:</strong> Obtaining copper(II) sulfate crystals</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Slower cooling = larger, purer crystals</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Crystallization Steps:</h4>\n            <ol class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>1. Heat solution to concentrate (don't dry completely)</li>\n              <li>2. Allow to cool slowly</li>\n              <li>3. Crystals form as solubility decreases</li>\n              <li>4. Filter to collect crystals</li>\n              <li>5. Dry between filter papers</li>\n            </ol>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Chromatography -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Chromatography\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-100 to-pink-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-1\">Principle</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Separates substances based on their <strong class=\"text-purple-600\">different solubilities</strong> in a solvent and their attraction to the paper/stationary phase.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Paper Chromatography Procedure:</h4>\n            <ol class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\"><span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">1</span> Draw a pencil line near bottom of paper</li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\"><span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">2</span> Place spot of mixture on the line</li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\"><span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">3</span> Dip paper in solvent (below the spot)</li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\"><span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">4</span> Solvent rises, carrying components at different speeds</li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\"><span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">5</span> Different components separate as spots at different heights</li>\n            </ol>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Rf Value</h4>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded font-mono text-center mb-2\">\n              Rf = Distance traveled by substance / Distance traveled by solvent\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Rf values identify substances (same compound = same Rf under same conditions)</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Other Methods -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n          Other Separation Methods\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -magnet mr-2\" data-mi=\"attractions\">attractions</span>Magnetic Separation</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Separates magnetic materials from non-magnetic.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-red-600 text-sm\"><strong>Example:</strong> Iron from sulfur</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -tint mr-2\" data-mi=\"water_drop\">water_drop</span>Separating Funnel</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Separates immiscible liquids (different densities).</p>\n            <p class=\"text-blue-600 text-sm\"><strong>Example:</strong> Oil and water</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -wind mr-2\" data-mi=\"air\">air</span>Sublimation</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Separates substances that sublime from those that don't.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-600 text-sm\"><strong>Example:</strong> Iodine, ammonium chloride</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -sync mr-2\" data-mi=\"sync\">sync</span>Centrifugation</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Spins mixtures at high speed; denser particles settle.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-purple-600 text-sm\"><strong>Example:</strong> Separating blood cells from plasma</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 7: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-cyan-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. How would you separate sand from salt?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside\">\n                  <li>Add water to dissolve salt</li>\n                  <li>Filter to remove sand (residue)</li>\n                  <li>Evaporate filtrate to obtain salt</li>\n                </ol>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Which method separates: (a) Oil and water, (b) Ink colors, (c) Salt from seawater?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>(a) <strong>Separating funnel</strong> - immiscible liquids</p>\n                <p>(b) <strong>Chromatography</strong> - separates dyes</p>\n                <p>(c) <strong>Distillation</strong> or <strong>Evaporation</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Why is crystallization used instead of evaporation for copper(II) sulfate?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Copper(II) sulfate decomposes on strong heating. Crystallization allows recovery without decomposition, and produces pure crystals.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. A substance travels 4 cm while the solvent travels 10 cm. What is its Rf value?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Rf = 4/10 = <strong>0.4</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-8\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-50 to-teal-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-cyan-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-cyan-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-cyan-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>Filtration:</strong> Insoluble solid from liquid (residue + filtrate)</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Distillation:</strong> Liquid from solution (based on boiling points)</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Fractional distillation:</strong> Miscible liquids with different boiling points</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Evaporation:</strong> Recover dissolved solid (if heat-stable)</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Crystallization:</strong> For solids that decompose on heating</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Chromatography:</strong> Separates based on solubility (Rf values)</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Separating funnel:</strong> Immiscible liquids (different densities)</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-cyan-50 to-teal-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card { transition: all 0.2s ease; }\n    .step-card:hover { transform: translateX(4px); }\n    #topic-complete-btn { transition: all 0.3s ease; }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover { transform: scale(1.02); }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"separation-techniques","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"Which method separates an insoluble solid from a liquid?","options":["Distillation","Filtration","Chromatography","Evaporation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Filtration separates insoluble solids (residue) from liquids (filtrate)."},{"question":"The liquid that passes through filter paper is called:","options":["Residue","Filtrate","Distillate","Solute"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Filtrate is the liquid that passes through; residue is the solid left behind."},{"question":"Which is used to separate miscible liquids with different boiling points?","options":["Filtration","Simple distillation","Fractional distillation","Separating funnel"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Fractional distillation separates miscible liquids using a fractionating column."},{"question":"Why is crystallization preferred over evaporation for some substances?","options":["It's faster","The solid doesn't decompose","It produces larger crystals","It's cheaper"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Crystallization is used for substances that decompose on heating."},{"question":"In chromatography, what does Rf value measure?","options":["Color intensity","Distance ratio of substance to solvent","Boiling point","Solubility"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Rf = distance traveled by substance ÷ distance traveled by solvent."},{"question":"Oil and water can be separated using:","options":["Filtration","Distillation","Separating funnel","Chromatography"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Oil and water are immiscible liquids - use separating funnel."},{"question":"Sublimation can separate:","options":["Salt from water","Iron from sulfur","Iodine from sand","Oil from water"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Iodine sublimes (solid → gas directly), so it can be separated from non-subliming solids."},{"question":"What is the solid left on filter paper called?","options":["Filtrate","Residue","Distillate","Precipitate"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Residue is the solid that remains on the filter paper after filtration."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"separation-techniques","topicTitle":"Separation Techniques","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7","section-8"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}